{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"agent_message","text":"The exact-layout experiment reduced register use from 44 to 39 VGPRs but generated less efficient memory code and was slower, so it will not replace the baseline. I’m checking one additional representation optimization: retaining the FP32 sum in FP16 registers between reduction and output. BF16 inputs in the workload’s ordinary numeric range generally sum exactly (or nearly exactly) in FP16; I’ll reject it unless direct error testing remains safely inside tolerance and it materially improves speed."}}
