{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"FP16 retention is numerically safe on direct tests (100% of elements satisfy the workload tolerance), and it cuts VGPR use from 44 to 38, but it does not improve the bandwidth-bound large cases. Its only meaningful gain is around batch 539. I’m testing whether that lower register pressure enables a smaller cooperative group—and therefore more resident rows per CU—before deciding whether any shape-specific dispatch is worthwhile."}}
