{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"agent_message","text":"Eight waves remains the most robust geometry; alternatives are effectively tied for large batches and slightly worse elsewhere. One remaining structural idea is reducing workgroup scheduling overhead on the 12k–14k-row cases by processing 2–4 rows sequentially per program. I’ll benchmark that locally and retain it only if it wins consistently; each row still performs the full exact computation."}}
